(_To preserve Apricots_.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Take your apricots and pare them, then stone what you can whole; give) Tj T*
(them a light boiling in a pint of water, or according to your quantity) Tj T*
(of fruit; then take the weight of your apricots in sugar, and take the) Tj T*
(liquor which you boil them in, and your sugar, and boil it till it) Tj T*
(comes to a sirrup, and give them a light boiling, taking of the scum) Tj T*
(as it rises; when the sirrup jellies, it is enough; then take up the) Tj T*
(apricots, and cover them with the jelly, and put cut paper over them,) Tj T*
(and lay them down when cold. Or, take you plumbs before they have) Tj T*
