(_To keep Damsons_.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Take damsons when they are first ripe, pick them off carefully, wipe) Tj T*
(them clean, put them into snuff bottles, stop them up tight so that no) Tj T*
(air can get to them, nor water; put nothing into the bottles but) Tj T*
(plumbs, put the bottles into cold water, hang them over the fire, let) Tj T*
(them heat slowly, let the water boil slowly for half an hour, when the) Tj T*
(water is cold take out the bottles, set the bottles into a cold place,) Tj T*
(they will keep twelve months if the bottles are stopped tight, so as) Tj T*
(no air nor water can get to them. They will not keep long after the) Tj T*
(bottles are opened; the plumbs must be hard.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
