() Tj T*
(Take the fairest and ripest peaches, pare them into fair water; take) Tj T*
(their weight in double refined sugar; of one half make a very thin) Tj T*
(sirrup; then put in your peaches, boiling them till they look clear,) Tj T*
(then split and stone them, boil them till they are very tender, lay) Tj T*
(them a draining, take the other half of the sugar, and boil it almost) Tj T*
(to a candy; then put in your peaches, and let them lie all night then) Tj T*
(lay them on a glass, and set them in a stove, till they are dry, if) Tj T*
